<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>All the news about Africa - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:43:23 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>France-Morocco rapprochement overshadowed by fresh Pegasus spying claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260718-france-morocco-rapprochement-overshadowed-by-fresh-pegasus-spying-claims</link><description>
As France seeks to rebuild ties with Morocco after years of diplomatic tensions, a new investigation claims Moroccan intelligence targeted senior French officials with Israeli-made Pegasus spyware. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c93201a-81df-11f1-8ec7-d771ed8df869</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:42:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>At least 20 children and one adult killed in school bus crash in Uganda</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260717-at-least-20-children-and-one-adult-killed-in-school-bus-crash-in-uganda</link><description>
At least 20 children and one adult have been killed after a bus carrying pupils home from a school trip crashed in eastern Uganda, police said on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f7499d4-81c1-11f1-b93b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Uganda-schoolbus-accident.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f7499d4-81c1-11f1-b93b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Uganda-schoolbus-accident.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6e46cd20-81c5-11f1-a018-1f0843f75d2d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:52:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f7499d4-81c1-11f1-b93b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Uganda-schoolbus-accident.jpg">© Uganda Police Force on X</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>G7 and EU call for halt to attacks in Sudan's El-Obeid and wider arms embargo</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260717-g7-and-eu-call-for-halt-to-attacks-in-sudan-s-el-obeid-and-wider-arms-embargo</link><description>
G7 foreign ministers and the European Union's foreign policy chief on Wednesday urged Sudan's Rapid Support Forces and allied armed groups to halt all actions that could lead to further atrocities or endanger civilians in El-Obeid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6233f044-8026-11f1-8398-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/SUDAN-displaced-women-from-El-Obeid-UN-rtrs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6233f044-8026-11f1-8398-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/SUDAN-displaced-women-from-El-Obeid-UN-rtrs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">32cce53c-8025-11f1-8067-c59f182dddbd</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 08:54:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6233f044-8026-11f1-8398-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/SUDAN-displaced-women-from-El-Obeid-UN-rtrs.jpg">REUTERS - El Tayeb Siddig</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>UN campaign trail takes former president Macky Sall back to Senegal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260717-un-campaign-trail-takes-former-president-macky-sall-back-to-senegal</link><description>
Senegal's former president Macky Sall returns home on Friday for the first time since leaving office in April 2024, in a visit tied to his bid to become the next UN secretary-general. But opponents say the violence that marked the final months of his mandate should disqualify him from the role.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6048b00-8102-11f1-a9cf-e51ea97b6ed6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 05:05:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg">© REUTERS - Eduardo Munoz </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Greenpeace Africa demands halt to $17bn Kenya coastal oil refinery</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-greenpeace-demands-halt-to-dangote-s-17bn-kenya-coastal-refinery</link><description>
Climate rights group Greenpeace Africa has called for a halt to a proposed oil refinery project by Africa's richest man, Aliko Dangote, in Kenya's coastal region, warning of the environmental risks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4ba7b34-8119-11f1-b689-57e3f657aba9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:29:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg">AFP - TONY KARUMBA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Students in Cameroon protest new financial requirements for French visas</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-cameroonian-students-protest-new-french-visa-financial-rules</link><description>
Dozens of people took to the streets outside the French embassy in Yaoundé this week to protest new rules that require Cameroonian nationals to demonstrate the means to pay tuition fees in full before they can obtain a student visa for France. Protesters say the policy will make studying in France impossible for many people who already have places at French institutions for the coming academic year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7cab886-8028-11f1-95bb-a97de1dfa122</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:56:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg">© RFI / Emmanuel Jules Ntap</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Lawyers vow to fight on after Kenya court rejects Rastafarians' cannabis bid</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-lawyers-vow-to-fight-on-after-kenya-court-rejects-rastafarians-cannabis-bid</link><description>
In a long-awaited ruling, Kenya's High Court has rejected a bid by Rastafarians to be allowed to smoke cannabis as part of their religious worship. But lawyers say the fight continues and the case has opened up debate on the country's drug laws and what constitutes religious freedom. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35d997e-7f66-11f1-9e5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84DG86B.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35d997e-7f66-11f1-9e5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84DG86B.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">69cb1838-802a-11f1-b21e-e9047a96864f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 10:12:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35d997e-7f66-11f1-9e5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84DG86B.jpg">AFP - SIMON MAINA</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ebola cases in DRC may be four times official tally, says WHO</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260715-congo-s-ebola-cases-may-be-four-times-official-tally-who-says</link><description>
The true number of Ebola cases in the Democratic Republic of Congo is at least double, and possibly four times, the official tally, the World Health Organization's emergencies chief said on Tuesday. Official figures say the fever has infected nearly 2,000 people since mid-May. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ad2a84a-7f8b-11f1-8951-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13-EBOLA-VACCINES-RTRs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ad2a84a-7f8b-11f1-8951-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13-EBOLA-VACCINES-RTRs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3be3d16-7f8a-11f1-85e1-69386237b861</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:08:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ad2a84a-7f8b-11f1-8951-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13-EBOLA-VACCINES-RTRs.jpg">REUTERS - Gradel Muyisa Mumbere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ethiopia 'closely engaged' over citizens facing execution in Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260714-ethiopia-closely-engaged-over-citizens-facing-execution-in-saudi-arabia</link><description>
Ethiopia says it's continuing "sustained diplomatic and consular efforts" to help dozens of its citizens facing the death penalty in Saudi Arabia, after an international rights group warned that at least 58 Ethiopian migrants are at imminent risk of execution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0484b668-7f7c-11f1-be68-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20043577409446.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0484b668-7f7c-11f1-be68-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20043577409446.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f14d2d7a-7f74-11f1-b090-5797132e4456</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:43:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0484b668-7f7c-11f1-be68-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20043577409446.jpg">AP - Nariman El-Mofty</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>In Zimbabwe, community seed banks are reviving indigenous crops</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260712-in-zimbabwe-community-seed-banks-are-reviving-indigenous-crops</link><description>
Zimbabwean farmers are reviving drought-resistant traditional crops through a community seed bank, helping them cope with worsening climate variability. The initiative, rooted in indigenous knowledge, is strengthening food security and offering a safety net against future droughts and floods.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5c81e88-7620-11f1-bb52-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Smallholder-farmers-sorting-seeds-of-small-grains-in-Chipinge-Credit-FAO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5c81e88-7620-11f1-bb52-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Smallholder-farmers-sorting-seeds-of-small-grains-in-Chipinge-Credit-FAO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83ce4e20-7621-11f1-8440-594032ce8249</guid><pubDate>Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:57:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c5c81e88-7620-11f1-bb52-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Smallholder-farmers-sorting-seeds-of-small-grains-in-Chipinge-Credit-FAO.jpg">© FAO</source><dc:creator>Farai Shawn Matiashe</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Relations between Algeria and Mali thaw after year-long rift over drone</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260711-relations-between-algeria-and-mali-thaw-after-year-long-rift-over-drone</link><description>
Mali and Algeria have reopened their airspace to each other's planes and reinstated their ambassadors, the countries have announced, more than a year after the destruction of a Malian drone strained relations between the neighbours.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f199ccbe-2b3a-11f0-b2e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_426D8WR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f199ccbe-2b3a-11f0-b2e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_426D8WR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4a74d28-7d06-11f1-b2ff-1b5a90cdefe5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:12:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f199ccbe-2b3a-11f0-b2e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000_426D8WR.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Fifteen years of independence for South Sudan, but still little to celebrate</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260709-fifteen-years-of-independence-for-south-sudan-but-still-little-to-celebrate</link><description>
South Sudan, the world's youngest country, on Thursday marks the 15th anniversary of its independence, following decades of war with Sudan, a 2005 peace agreement and a 2011 self-determination referendum in which almost 99 percent of voters backed statehood. But the hopes that came with it have given way to renewed conflict, economic collapse and political deadlock.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81c8ec0c-3e3b-11f1-a84b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-338G3TH.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81c8ec0c-3e3b-11f1-a84b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-338G3TH.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">50db48b0-7b85-11f1-88d8-7fc8d62dffcc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 21:06:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/81c8ec0c-3e3b-11f1-a84b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-338G3TH.jpg">AFP - TIZIANA FABI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Zimbabwe's ruling party accused of hollowing out parliamentary oversight</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260709-zimbabwe-s-ruling-party-accused-of-hollowing-out-parliamentary-oversight</link><description>
Zimbabwean President Emmerson Mnangagwa has signed into law constitutional changes extending his time in office from 2028 to 2030. The legislation, known as CAB3, also allows parliament, rather than a public vote, to elect future presidents. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e2f7699e-3301-11f1-93e6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Emmerson-Mnangagwa.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e2f7699e-3301-11f1-93e6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Emmerson-Mnangagwa.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f8c4e6e-7ad6-11f1-b170-8f353acd979b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 12:38:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e2f7699e-3301-11f1-93e6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Emmerson-Mnangagwa.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>Anne-Marie Bissada</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>'We have our own local identity’: Morocco's Jazzablanca festival founder</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260709-we-have-our-own-local-identity-morocco-s-jazzablanca-festival-founder</link><description>
As the Jazzablanca festival celebrates its 19th edition, RFI spoke to its founder Moulay Ahmed Alami about how the event has evolved, its support for Moroccan artists and the wider cultural and economic impact on Casablanca.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4dff1ec6-7abf-11f1-b21e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Moulay-Ahmed-Alami-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4dff1ec6-7abf-11f1-b21e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Moulay-Ahmed-Alami-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d84f74e-7a17-11f1-bb2d-d19d2f0f8ff6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 08:41:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4dff1ec6-7abf-11f1-b21e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Moulay-Ahmed-Alami-1.jpg">© RFI/I. Martinetti</source><dc:creator>Isabelle Martinetti</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ugandan farmers take TotalEnergies' pipeline to UK court</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260708-ugandan-farmers-launch-uk-case-against-pipeline-oil-project-led-by-totalenergies</link><description>
Four Ugandan farmers filed a case against the East African Crude Oil Pipeline (EACOP) at the UK's High Court on Tuesday, seeking to have Ugandan constitutional, environmental and climate law applied to EACOP Ltd, the UK-registered company financing the project
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c275f3b0-0f6d-11f0-93da-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EACOP%20Protester%20Uganda-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c275f3b0-0f6d-11f0-93da-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EACOP%20Protester%20Uganda-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">530268ae-79e5-11f1-a4c6-13d92c0fb746</guid><pubDate>Wed, 08 Jul 2026 20:06:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c275f3b0-0f6d-11f0-93da-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EACOP%20Protester%20Uganda-1.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Kenya journalist escapes abduction after criticism of president, says CPJ</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260708-kenya-journalist-escapes-abduction-after-criticism-of-president-says-cpj</link><description>
The Committee to Protect Journalists has called for an investigation into the attempted kidnapping of a senior journalist in Kenya, which followed angry criticism of his newspaper by President William Ruto.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ab4dfcbe-79fc-11f1-b648-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Kenya-The-Standard-Newspaper-000-32GL6JZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ab4dfcbe-79fc-11f1-b648-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Kenya-The-Standard-Newspaper-000-32GL6JZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e7e6294-79f5-11f1-9c85-b373ab8f581c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 08 Jul 2026 10:44:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ab4dfcbe-79fc-11f1-b648-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Kenya-The-Standard-Newspaper-000-32GL6JZ.jpg">AFP - SIMON MAINA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight on Africa</category><title>Climate justice in Africa: floods, fossil fuels and the fightback</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/spotlight-on-africa/20260707-climate-justice-in-africa-floods-fossil-fuels-and-the-fightback</link><description>
This week in Spotlight on Africa, we look at climate change, environmental justice and the challenges of adaptation. While Europe's heatwaves make headlines, temperatures are also climbing across Africa, with parts of the Sahel approaching 50°C. West Africa is also experiencing severe flooding caused by climate change. Yet Africa is also a source of innovation and solutions, as we'll be discussing today.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/585d91be-4af3-11f1-b2ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2-e-waka-electric-bikes-IMG-2518.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/585d91be-4af3-11f1-b2ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2-e-waka-electric-bikes-IMG-2518.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ff358e2-709d-11f1-a187-d3dd50c4a29b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2026 12:27:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Melissa Chemam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rebels seize key town of Anéfis as they tighten grip on northern Mali</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260706-rebels-seize-key-town-of-an%C3%A9fis-as-rebels-tighten-grip-on-northern-mali</link><description>
Tuareg separatists and al-Qaeda affiliates appear to have secured control of a key town in northern Mali following a coordinated offensive by the rebels over the weekend. The Malian army and Russian mercenaries have been holed up in the key camp of Anéfis after the rebels launched their offensive on Saturday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/10dcd586-7940-11f1-ad64-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B2HR4MZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/10dcd586-7940-11f1-ad64-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B2HR4MZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f83222f6-792c-11f1-9587-65df0bac37ec</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 17:16:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/10dcd586-7940-11f1-ad64-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B2HR4MZ.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>Anne-Marie Bissada</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Facing heavy security, Tanzania protesters fear repeat of election violence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260706-tanzania-protesters-face-heavy-security-fear-repeat-of-deadly-election-violence</link><description>
Tanzanians planning to protest on Tuesday against government repression are facing a heavy police presence and warnings from authorities, which recalls the mass killings that followed last October's disputed election.
